---
import AcademyScene from "./AcademyScene.astro";
import FieldOperation from "./FieldOperation.astro";
import PassportTools from "./PassportTools.astro";
import {roles,missionRoleBrief,missionFacts,recoveryProfiles,missionFieldSpec,newMission,type MissionKind} from "../lib/mission-engine";
import {missionSummaries} from "../data/learner-guidance";
import {withBase} from "astro-theme-university/url";
import "../styles/learner-guidance.css";
interface Props {kind?:MissionKind}
const {kind="recovery"}=Astro.props;
const guide=missionSummaries[kind];
const facts=kind==="recovery"?missionFacts.recovery:missionFacts.a1;
const fieldSpec=missionFieldSpec(newMission(kind));
const title=kind==="a1"?"The Sealed Workshop":kind==="a2"?"Restore the Relay":"Operation Last Light";
---
<section class="mission" data-mission={kind} aria-label={title+" playable trial"}>
 <header class="mission-intro"><div><p class="eyebrow">PLAYABLE {kind==="recovery"?"FINAL MISSION":"ASSESSMENT"}</p><h2>{title}</h2><p>{kind==="a1"?"Investigate an unfamiliar workshop. Select inspections, predict a useful test and explain a supported release; use notes or recall as appropriate.":kind==="a2"?"A silent relay, a faulty circuit and two competing records. Restore the signal through precise collaboration.":"The last intact research archive is inside Meridian Station. Recover it without losing what makes it worth recovering."}</p></div><span class="mission-seal" aria-hidden="true">M<br/>/27</span></header>
 <p class="learner-orientation"><strong>Your operation:</strong> inspect the mission console to discover the problem. Explore the labelled areas, use their equipment and test your reasoning. A verified solution changes what the field console can do. Then perform the release, transmission or support handover and finish at the receiving point. Walk or tap the floor in 3D; the equivalent field buttons work with keyboard and touch. Keep full screen open throughout.</p>
 <AcademyScene room="meridian" mode="mission" contextId={'mission:'+kind} />
 <div data-immersive-panel="mission">
 <p data-legacy-mission hidden class="mission-status" role="status"></p>
 <section class="learner-guide" aria-label="Mission instructions">
  <p class="eyebrow">{kind==="recovery"?"FINAL PROJECT":"ASSESSMENT"} / PRACTICAL TRIAL</p>
  <h3>Your mission</h3><p>{guide.goal}</p>
  <p class="small">The trial is ready to play. Your actions save locally as you go. Solo practice allows role switching; pairs and teams can share a screen and rotate control.</p>
  <div class="learner-next">
   <p class="eyebrow" data-mission-next-label>{kind==="recovery"?"AVAILABLE CHECK / OPTIONAL GUIDANCE":"DO THIS NEXT"}</p>
   <h4 data-mission-next-title>Inspect the mission console</h4>
   <p data-mission-next-action>{fieldSpec.problem} Inspect it before beginning the equipment work.</p>
   <p class="small" data-mission-next-success>Done when the mission console records your inspection and reveals the equipment needed.</p>
   <button type="button" data-mission-next disabled>Focus the mission console</button>
  </div>
 </section>
 {kind==="recovery"&&<label class="mission-approach">Approach to perform<select data-field-ending><option value="physical">Carry the original to Dispatch</option><option value="digital">Transmit a verified digital copy</option><option value="stabilise">Hold the original stable and hand over</option></select><span class="small">Changing approach preserves the initial objective and skill evidence; perform the new approach before filing its outcome.</span></label>}
 <FieldOperation spec={fieldSpec} scope={"mission:"+kind} />
 <div class="mission-setup"><label>Scenario for next trial<select data-scenario><option value="baseline">Baseline</option><option value="equipment-failure">Equipment failure</option><option value="conflicting-archive">Conflicting archive</option></select></label><label hidden={kind!=="recovery"}>Declared recovery objective<select data-objective><option value="physical">Recover physical archive</option><option value="digital">Recover verified digital copy</option><option value="stabilise">Stabilise for handover</option></select></label><button type="button" data-start-mission disabled>Start new trial</button><span class="small">Changing Scenario takes effect when you select Start new trial. Saved trials resume automatically; starting over keeps completed records. For a new final-project run, choose its objective before the first practical action.</span></div>
 <div class="mission-rolebar" role="group" aria-label="Choose your role">{Object.entries(roles).map(([id,r])=><button type="button" data-role={id} disabled aria-pressed={id==="observer"}>{r.title}</button>)}</div>
 <details class="role-brief"><summary data-role-title>Observer / Navigator briefing</summary><p data-role-brief>{missionRoleBrief("observer",kind)}</p><p class="small" data-role-tools></p><a href="#role-packs">Read all role packs</a></details>
 <div class="mission-grid">
  <aside class="mission-objectives"><p class="eyebrow">MISSION JOURNAL</p><h3>Required objectives</h3><p data-mission-progress class="small"></p><p data-mission-scope class="small"></p><p class="small">Choose your investigation order. The suggested next objective locates available controls; it is not a compulsory walkthrough. In your plan, justify necessary checks and explain any omissions.</p><details class="learner-checklist"><summary>All objectives and instructions</summary><ol data-objectives></ol></details><p class="small">A tick records a practical condition met. It is not an academic grade. Changing equipment can reopen a dependent objective.</p></aside>
  <div class="mission-console">
   <nav class="zone-tabs" aria-label="Station areas">
    {[["arrival","01 Arrival"],["workshop","02 Workshop"],["power","03 Power bay"],["control","04 Control room"],["archive","05 Archive"],["dispatch","06 Dispatch"]].map(([id,label])=><button type="button" data-zone={id} disabled>{label}</button>)}
   </nav>
   <h3 class="learner-console-title">Room controls and feedback</h3>
   <p role="status" data-mission-status class="mission-status">Your saved mission is loading. The instructions and role packs are available below.</p>
   <section data-zone-panel="arrival"><p class="learner-role-note">Use Observer / Navigator for all three tasks in this room.</p><p class="eyebrow">OBSERVATION · MEMORY · SPATIAL REASONING</p><h3>The room is your first instrument.</h3><p>Inspect the inventory and source records needed for your claim. Notes remain available. Recall is optional; explain when it helps and when a written record is more dependable. Transport planning needs the map; stationary outcomes do not.</p><div class="actions">{["lens","spool","tile","map","manifest"].map(item=><button type="button" data-inspect={item}>Inspect {item}</button>)}</div><p data-inspection class="inspection-note"></p><button type="button" data-hide-manifest>Hide inspection notes</button><form data-recall><p class="small">Optional recall practice; it never blocks this assessment.</p><label>Recall the packing order<input name="items" autocomplete="off" placeholder="item, item, item" required maxlength="100"/></label><button>Check recall</button></form><form data-orient><label>Clockwise rotation of north<select name="degrees"><option value="0">0°</option><option value="90">90°</option><option value="180">180°</option><option value="270">270°</option></select></label><button>Test orientation</button></form></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="workshop" hidden><p class="learner-role-note">Use Systems Specialist to change gears, release the brake and turn the crank.</p><p class="eyebrow">MECHANICAL DIAGNOSIS</p><h3>The recovery cradle.</h3><p data-cradle-instruction>{kind==="recovery"?"A twelve-tooth driver must produce the output required by the verified archive profile. Use output = driver teeth ÷ follower teeth. Diagnose the holding and gearing conditions independently; this apparatus is needed for physical transport or continuing support.":"A twelve-tooth input gear drives the cam. The cradle requires half-speed output in the opposite direction. Inspect the interlock before applying another turn."}</p><p data-profile-status class="inspection-note" hidden={kind!=="recovery"}>Verify the archive profile in the Control room before testing the final cradle.</p><label>Follower gear<select data-follower><option value="36">36 teeth</option><option value="24">24 teeth</option><option value="48">48 teeth</option></select></label><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" data-brake/> Release the holding brake</label><button type="button" data-turn>Turn input once</button><output data-mechanism-readout></output></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="power" hidden><p class="learner-role-note">Use Systems Specialist. Measure the original fault before replacing it.</p><p class="eyebrow">ELECTRONICS · MEASUREMENT</p><h3>A complete path.</h3><p>The training supply is 6 V. Power flows through the fuse, switch, lamp and return. Find the break before replacing anything.</p><button type="button" data-measure>Measure supply and fuse</button><output data-measurement></output><label>Replacement fuse<select data-fuse><option value="open">No replacement installed</option><option value="intact">Intact fuse</option></select></label><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" data-switch/> Close the load switch</label><p data-circuit-readout></p></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="control" hidden><p class="learner-role-note">Use Investigator for the archive comparison and permission repair.</p><p class="eyebrow">DIGITAL INVESTIGATION · PERMISSIONS</p><h3>Which copy can you justify?</h3><div data-archive-records></div><form data-replica><label>Copy matching the current signed source<select name="replica"><option value="A">Archive A</option><option value="B">Archive B</option></select></label><button>Verify selected archive</button></form><details open><summary>Fictional application: permission defect</summary><p>Observer/read is allowed. Technician/service is allowed. Registrar/certify is allowed. Compare that mandate with the installed entries: observer/read ALLOW; observer/certify ALLOW; technician/service ALLOW; registrar/certify ALLOW. Derive which change is justified.</p><form data-policy><label>Subject<select name="subject"><option value="observer">Observer</option><option value="technician">Technician</option><option value="registrar">Registrar</option></select></label><label>Action<select name="action"><option value="certify">Certify</option><option value="read">Read</option><option value="service">Service</option></select></label><label>New decision<select name="decision"><option value="deny">Deny</option><option value="allow">Allow</option></select></label><button>Apply policy and run checks</button></form></details></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="archive" hidden><p class="learner-role-note">{kind==="a2"?"Use Coordinator to complete the three handoff fields. Agreement and route are final-project tasks.":"Use Coordinator for agreement and handoff; switch to Observer / Navigator for the route."}</p><p class="eyebrow">COMMUNICATION · NEGOTIATION · NAVIGATION</p><h3>An agreement that can be acted on.</h3><blockquote>“Preserve the original. Tell me who receives the archive. Then we can agree a recovery.”<cite>— Meridian custodian</cite></blockquote><form data-agreement><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="preserve"/> Commit to preserving the original</label><label>Named handover recipient<input name="recipient" maxlength="100" placeholder="Name or assigned team role" required/></label><button>Negotiate handling agreement</button></form>{kind==="a2"&&<p data-relay-receiving-card class="inspection-note">Switch to Coordinator to inspect the receiver’s acceptance card. The sending analyst holds the source evidence; exchange the relevant facts.</p>}<form data-handoff><label>Item<select name="item"><option value="archive">Archive</option><option value="verified archive">Verified archive</option></select></label><label>Destination<select name="destination"><option value="workshop">Workshop</option><option value="dispatch">Dispatch</option></select></label><label>Condition<select name="condition"><option value="immediately">Immediately</option><option value="after integrity check">After integrity check</option></select></label>{kind==="a2"&&<label>Receiver’s read-back code<input name="acknowledgement" required maxlength="100" autocomplete="off" placeholder="Ask the receiving role for its current code"/></label>}<button>Send structured handoff</button></form><h4>Route model</h4><p>Upper and lift routes depend on the lift supply. The service passage is independent and includes two marked sensor pauses. Consult the scenario bulletin before committing.</p><p data-disruption class="scenario-bulletin"></p><form data-route><label>Route<select name="route"><option value="upper">Upper passage</option><option value="service">Service passage</option><option value="lift">Lift</option></select></label><button>Test route dependencies</button></form></section>
   <section data-zone-panel="dispatch" hidden><details data-mission-plan-notes open={kind==="recovery"}><summary>{kind==="recovery"?"Your original plan and revisions":"Optional planning notes and preserved versions"}</summary><p class="learner-role-note">Use Coordinator to preserve your plan versions. Any role can finish once the required objectives are met.</p><p class="eyebrow">PLANNING · ADAPTATION · DEFENCE</p><h3>Keep the decisions, including the ones you changed.</h3><p>Record an original plan before your revision. A revision should explain a new observation, a tested assumption or a changed condition. Earlier versions remain intact. A changed approach requires a new version; name why its checks are needed, which can be omitted and what remains unresolved.</p><form data-plan><label>Plan or revision<textarea name="text" rows="4" minlength="20" maxlength="8000" required placeholder="Route, evidence, responsibilities, and why this version makes sense…"></textarea></label><button>Preserve this plan version</button></form><div data-plans></div></details>{kind==="recovery"&&<section class="resolution-evidence" aria-label="Evidence for your chosen ending"><h4>Evidence for your chosen ending</h4><p>Complete the conditions required by your chosen objective, perform your selected field operation and then record the outcome you actually achieved. These checks confirm the record is present and matches the model; your written defence explains its quality.</p><form data-resolution-evidence><label>Outcome to document<select name="ending" data-outcome-choice><option value="physical">Physical recovery</option><option value="digital">Verified digital recovery</option><option value="stabilise">Stabilisation and handover</option></select></label><label>Responsible recipient<input name="recipient" required minlength="2" maxlength="100" placeholder="Named custodian or receiving role"/></label><fieldset data-outcome-fields="physical"><legend>Physical custody and support</legend><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="support" required/> I confirm the verified profile's cradle and selected route have been tested for this transfer.</label><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="preserve-physical" required/> I acknowledge original-preserving custody with the named recipient.</label></fieldset><fieldset data-outcome-fields="digital" hidden><legend>Verified receipt and retained original</legend><p data-digital-receipt>Transmit the verified copy and collect the receiving receipt from the field terminal.</p><label>Verified receipt code<input name="receipt" maxlength="100" required/></label><label>Original retained at<input name="digital-location" minlength="3" maxlength="100" required placeholder="Recorded station location"/></label><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="preserve-digital" required/> I confirm the original remains preserved at this location.</label></fieldset><fieldset data-outcome-fields="stabilise" hidden><legend>Stable handover and remaining work</legend><label class="choice-label"><input type="checkbox" name="stable" required/> I confirm the tested equipment supports a stable archive pending handover.</label><label>Stable archive location<input name="stable-location" minlength="3" maxlength="100" required/></label></fieldset><label>Scope, alternative and remaining obligation<textarea name="limitation" minlength="20" maxlength="2000" rows="4" required placeholder="Why did these checks matter? Which could you omit and why? What credible alternative did you reject? What must the recipient do next?"></textarea></label><p class="small">For stabilisation, name a monitoring responsibility and a condition that requires escalation. For digital recovery, explain how the retained original remains protected. For physical recovery, explain custody and transport limits. The minimum length is a presence check; a tutor evaluates the reasoning.</p><button>Record outcome evidence</button></form><p data-outcome-status role="status">No outcome evidence recorded yet.</p></section>}
   <h4>{kind==="recovery"?"File the completed recovery":"Complete the trial record"}</h4><div class="ending-choices">{kind==="recovery"?<><button type="button" data-ending="physical">File physical recovery record</button><button type="button" data-ending="digital">File digital recovery record</button><button type="button" data-ending="stabilise">File stable handover record</button></>:<button type="button" data-ending={kind==="a1"?"physical":"digital"}>Finish {kind==="a1"?"workshop":"relay"} trial</button>}</div><p>These buttons record a completed operation; they cannot perform it for you. Finish the field handover first. No ending is an academic grade.</p></section>
  </div>
 </div>
 <section data-debrief data-immersive-reflection hidden class="mission-debrief"><p class="eyebrow">AFTER ACTION</p><h3 data-ending-title></h3><p data-ending-text></p><p>{guide.after}</p>{kind==="recovery"&&<p><a href={withBase("/sessions/week-12/#training-title-12")}>Continue to the Week 12 after-action account</a>. Your run stays saved; opening another page leaves full screen.</p>}<p>Now explain your observations and decisions using the exported action record. Compare a different scenario: which skill transferred, which assumption changed, and what remains uncertain?</p></section>
 <div class="actions"><button type="button" data-export-mission disabled>Export assessment record</button><button type="button" data-print-mission disabled>Print mission report</button></div>
 <details><summary>Action record and previous runs</summary><ol data-action-log></ol><div data-run-comparison></div></details>
 <section id="role-packs"><h3>Four roles. One shared operation.</h3><p>Use one browser, share a screen or rotate control. Solo students switch roles. Local role selections record practice responsibility, not verified identity.</p><div class="role-packs">{Object.entries(roles).map(([id,r])=><details><summary>{r.title}</summary><p>{missionRoleBrief(id as keyof typeof roles,kind)}</p><p>{r.tools.join(" · ")}</p></details>)}</div></section>
 <details><summary>Static mission worksheet and governing rules</summary><p>Use the assessment’s campus pack for a complete paper route. Record your objective, inspect the supplied inventory, compare sources and predict the result of each test before acting. Keep observations separate from interpretations. Notes are permitted; memorisation is optional.</p>
 <p>The workshop’s driver has twelve teeth. Output turns = driver teeth ÷ follower teeth × input turns, with the opposite direction. The holding brake blocks motion. The series supply connects source, fuse, switch, load and return; measurements distinguish a broken path from a mistaken equipment assumption. Isolate the supply before replacement.</p>
 <p>A complete archive must match the current signed source. A later timestamp does not establish authority. The handling mandate requires preservation of the original and a named responsible recipient. The permission mandate permits observer/read, technician/service and registrar/certify; compare installed entries against it. The receiving desk accepts a verified archive at Dispatch after its integrity check.</p>
 {kind==="recovery"?<><p>Profile A requires one-third output; profile B requires one-quarter output. Identify the current source before choosing any dependent support configuration. Physical recovery needs a viable transport route: Upper and Lift depend on the lift supply; Service is independent. The equipment-failure bulletin disables Upper and Lift.</p><p>Digital recovery needs transmission power and permission plus a matching receipt; the original stays in place. Stabilisation needs a tested support and continuous power, a stability indicator, named custodian and monitoring plan. Neither requires transporting the original. Publish the same role records and observations on paper; a facilitator reveals the selected test’s authored result, not a suggested repair.</p></>:<p>A1 requires a supported workshop release with orientation and a tested half-speed model. A2 requires diagnosed transmission power, a justified copy, correct permission and a receiver’s exact read-back. The assessment briefs identify supporting lab records and the independent written account.</p>}
 <p>Before filing an outcome, perform its release, transmission or support action and handover. Retain the action record, initial/revised plan, scope rationale and limitations. No ending supplies an academic grade.</p></details>
 <PassportTools />
 <dialog data-restart-dialog><h2>Start a new trial?</h2><p>The current in-progress trial will be replaced. Completed records and your lab passport remain. Export this run first if you need its unfinished record.</p><div class="actions"><button type="button" data-restart-confirm>Start new trial</button><button type="button" data-restart-cancel>Keep this trial</button></div></dialog>
 <pre class="mission-print-report" hidden data-mission-print></pre>
 </div>
 <noscript><p>The complete mission worksheet and role information above remain available. For interactive play, enable JavaScript or use the campus pack.</p></noscript>
</section>
<script>import "../scripts/mission-client";</script>